福田站，切开看 Futian, in Section — Miniature (微缩景观), a NEO-Cine library demo

An unofficial fan film about a real place, Futian Station in Shenzhen. It is not made, endorsed or checked by China State
Railway Group, Shenzhen Metro or any operator, and shows no operator logo or emblem. Station names, line numbers and line
colours are public facts; every date and fact on screen is sourced in FACTS.md.
THE SECTION IS A DIAGRAM: the three tiers (street with buses, metro, high-speed rail), their order, the platforms, the single
track on each tier and the escalators are artistic, not the station's real floors, tracks or transfer routes. Trains, the bus
and the people are illustrative, on invented timings. (The end card signs off with NEO-Cine only; this note is in DEMO.md.)

DESIGN SOURCE: the look and the model are adapted, with the author's consent, from the repository owner's own project
"福田站 · 精致微缩 v003" (refined miniature of Futian Station): the three-tier cut model, the bevelled parts, physical glass
and paint, the stone and wood micro-surfaces, the rounded tree crowns, the people, trains, bus, stairs, escalators and the
thin display plinth (demo/kit.js, demo/model.js, demo/main.js say what was taken and what was changed).

BUILDING DATA: data/city.json, made by neo/geo/buildings.py on 2026-11-13 for 114.0395–114.0530 E, 22.5340–22.5485 N:
  - OpenStreetMap, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0, https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
    (through the Overpass API);
  - Overture Maps Foundation, buildings theme, release 2026-10-21.0, ODbL 1.0, https://overturemaps.org; the footprints it adds
    here come from Qian Shi et al., "A First High-quality Vector Data of Buildings in East Asian Countries Based on a
    Comprehensive Large-scale Mapping Framework", Zenodo 2023, doi:10.5281/zenodo.8174931, CC BY 4.0.
  data/city.json is a derived database and stays under ODbL 1.0. The film is a produced work.
  How it is drawn: only the buildings west of Yitian Road, 45 to 560 m from the station's axis and between its two ends, as
  white massing at 1 model unit = 45 m (horizontally and vertically). Heights: 34 tagged, 73 from floor counts, 266 estimated
  by the script (capped at 60 m). The block keeps its real plan but is moved back by the depth of the section (in reality the
  station runs under the road directly beside it). No boundary of any kind is fetched or drawn.
LINE COLOURS: the `colour` tags of the OpenStreetMap route relations of Shenzhen Metro Lines 2, 3 and 11 (ODbL 1.0), fetched
  2026-11-13 through neo/geo/routes.py; no official colour code was found (FACTS.md).

FACTS: see FACTS.md (Shenzhen Transport Bureau, Futian District government, Shenzhen Metro, National Railway Administration,
  China News Service). Checked 2026-11-13.

PICTURE: built entirely in code with three.js r170 (MIT): procedural geometry, RoomEnvironment reflections, GTAO, a tilt-shift
  blur and bloom written for this film. No photographs, scans, AI-generated images, video or 3D model files.

SOUND: all synthesized for this film in mix.py: kalimba, music-box and harp voices by the library's core/audio/pluck.py;
  marimba, glass bell, pads, engines, rails, brakes, chimes, motors, clacks, paper, relay, hum, birds and crickets in numpy and
  through core/audio/sfx.py. The arrival chimes are generic two-note intervals, not any operator's real chime. No samples or
  recordings.

FONTS (SIL Open Font License 1.1; fetched by tools/fonts.sh from github.com/google/fonts at commit 86aced91, not kept in git;
  licence texts in fonts/):
- Inter (variable, Inter[opsz,wght].ttf), The Inter Project Authors: Latin text and figures.
- Noto Sans SC (variable, NotoSansSC[wght].ttf), Google / Adobe: Chinese text, subset by tools/subset.py to the characters
